{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Lodge here this night.</b> In the fullness of his pride and grandeur, the princes of Moab seemed to him lowly, and therefore he said to them לינו פה הלילה — a mere overnight lodging; but when they sent other envoys, many and more honored than these, he said to them שבו נא בזה, which is language of lingering, as in (Deuteronomy 1) ״ותשבו בקדש ימים רבים,״ and further he entreated them, for he added the word נא."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:56.683745100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}